## A Gmail address makes a real business look unfinished

Customers hesitate to trust an order confirmation, invoice, or reply from a
personal Gmail address instead of your own domain. An address like
`hello@yourbusiness.com` signals an established company, not a side project.

## It unlocks verification and payments

Business verification, payment gateways, and marketplace approvals often
require a business email. A branded address clears those checks faster.

## What it takes

If you already own the domain, setup is small: a few DNS records, an inbox,
and mobile app access. Most businesses are sending within a day — with
nothing technical on their end.

